# Privacy Policy — Kanji Extractor

---

## English

**Last updated: 24 June 2026**

Kanji Extractor ("the app", "the extension") is a browser extension that helps you
study Japanese by extracting kanji terms from the web page you are reading and
building a personal, frequency-ranked vocabulary history.

### Summary
- The app does **not** collect, sell, share, or transmit your data to the
  developer or to any third party.
- All processing happens **on your device**, and only after you click **Extract**.
- There are **no** analytics, trackers, advertising, accounts, or
  developer-operated servers.

### Data stored on your device
To build your vocabulary history, the app stores the following **locally on your
device** (in the browser's extension storage):
- the extracted kanji terms;
- an occurrence count and the first/last dates each term was seen;
- the address (URL) of the page where a term was first seen.

This information never leaves your device except through the optional iCloud sync
described below — and the page URL is **never** included in that sync.

### Optional iCloud sync (Safari only)
On Safari (macOS and iOS) you may turn on **iCloud sync** (it is **off by
default**). When enabled, your vocabulary history (the term, its count, and the
first/last seen dates) is stored in **your own private iCloud database (Apple
CloudKit)** so it can sync across your devices.
- This data lives in **your** iCloud account. The developer **cannot access it**.
- The page URLs are **not** synced; they remain on your device only.
- iCloud is provided by Apple and governed by Apple's Privacy Policy
  (https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/).
- Sync is available only on Safari. On Chrome and Firefox the app is **local
  only** and never syncs.

### No data collection by the developer
The app contains no analytics, crash reporting, advertising, or third-party SDKs,
and contacts no developer-operated server. The developer does not receive, store,
or have access to your browsing data, the extracted text, your vocabulary history,
or any personal information.

### Permissions
The extension requests only the access needed to read the **current** page's text
when you click Extract. It does not run in the background across your pages, and
it does not monitor your browsing.

### Children's privacy
The app does not collect any personal information from anyone, including children.

### Data retention and deletion
Your history stays on your device until you clear it from within the app. If
iCloud sync is on, clearing your history also removes the synced data from your
private iCloud database. You can additionally manage or delete iCloud data through
your device's iCloud settings.

### Changes to this policy
If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted at this address with a
revised "Last updated" date.

### Contact
Questions about this policy: tomas.social@gmail.com

